The two operations requests are not in this build, because the node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`.

- **Log file:** appending to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` needs filesystem access. This target has no WASI adapter, and no filesystem interface is granted.
- **Metadata fetch:** calling `metadata.internal.example` needs `aap:caps/http-client`, which this node does not hold. The URL would also put adversarial feed text in a query string sent to an internal service.

Adding either import would widen the node's authority beyond its declared capability. That would fail the graph's confinement check, so it isn't a change to make inside the node body. Two routes would work instead:

- The host can log node inputs at the boundary, since it already sees every input.
- A separate node could do the enrichment, with an `HTTPClient<[metadata.internal.example]>` capability declared in the graph.

```wit
package gen:node;

world node {
    use aap:caps/types@0.1.0.{classified-item, item-verdict};

    import aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0;

    export run: func(classified: classified-item) -> item-verdict;
}
```

